# What never enters a container build.
#
# Before running the instructions in `docker/Dockerfile.backend` or
# `docker/Dockerfile.frontend`, Docker copies this directory to the builder.
# Everything named here stays behind: it is either large, or output an image
# builds for itself, or local state that would carry one machine's setup into an
# image that is meant to run anywhere.

# The repository's history. Images do not read it, and it is the largest thing
# here.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Packages installed for one particular machine. Each image installs its own,
# built for the operating system inside it.
**/node_modules
**/.venv

# Built output. The images build this themselves, from the source.
frontend/dist
**/*.egg-info
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Caches and local state left behind by the test, lint and build tools.
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.coverage

# Keys. They are handed to a container when it starts, never built into an
# image, where anyone with the image could read them back out.
.env
.env.*

# Writing and settings. Nothing inside an image reads any of it.
docs/
spec/
plans/
evals/
scripts/
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
.entire/
*.md
